v2.0.0 rebuilt the Baccarat module as a local Python server application. v2.1.0-v2.4.0 added the Tie
bet and its own stake, the half-screen layout, PASS recording the table's result, and the OCR
groundwork. v2.5.x-v2.7.x built and proved the OCR tooling, calibration, the confidence gate and the
live loop. v2.8.x connected the setup screen to the reader, added one-click and drawn calibration,
fixed the drawing coordinate bug, and pre-measured the Pragmatic half-width profile. v2.9.x fixed the
reasons the live reader produced nothing and its latency, and adopted the roulette monitor's
wait-for-stillness method.

v2.10.0 is the user's idea, implemented: the white history grid left of the panels shows a hand's
result before the panels finish flashing, and each marker's colour IS the result (red Banker, blue
Player, green Tie). Reading it is a colour test — no model call, no API cost, ~0.25s — with the vision
model kept as the fallback. The grid's location is found automatically from the already-calibrated
panels region, so there is no second measurement to make.

The per-release record for the module is BACARAT/CHANGELOG.md.
